From 5b71e18e74465fdd9867d7ca1f8cce3b87fc9365 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 17:07:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: don't type-pun the immediate values through a cast

load_const() reads the caller's float array through a uint32_t pointer.
That is undefined behaviour, and gcc for arm reorders the read ahead of
the compound literal's store, so the immediate captures whatever the
stack held.  Whether the value survives depends on the compiler, the
target and inlining -- which is how the bug shipped: the miscompile only
happens in the 32-bit arm build that runs on the actual hardware, and
every immediate any a2xx shader uses is potentially affected.

Copy the values with memcpy instead.

Fixes: 67610a0323dd ("freedreno: a2xx: NIR backend")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/43606>

---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c
index 5cb1daf1b61..b09805f2167 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c
@@ -137,7 +137,14 @@ load_const(struct ir2_context *ctx, float *value_f, unsigned ncomp)
    unsigned idx, i, j;
    unsigned imm_ncomp = 0;
    unsigned swiz = 0;
-   uint32_t *value = (uint32_t *)value_f;
+   uint32_t value[4];
+
+   /* type-punned through memcpy: reading the caller's float array through
+    * a uint32_t pointer is undefined and gcc on arm reorders the read
+    * ahead of the store, turning the immediate into stack garbage
+    */
+   assert(ncomp <= ARRAY_SIZE(value));
+   memcpy(value, value_f, ncomp * sizeof(*value));
 
    /* try to merge with existing immediate (TODO: try with neg) */
    for (idx = 0; idx < so->num_immediates; idx++) {

